#
# NOTE on SOC_QEMU_VIRT_ARM64: this selects zephyr/soc/arm/qemu_virt_arm64,
# an upstream Zephyr SoC layer that -- despite its name -- is generic
# ARM64/Cortex-A/ARMv8-A glue (see its Kconfig.soc + mmu_regions.c): the only
# thing mmu_regions.c does is flat-map whatever GIC address the *board's own
# devicetree* declares, and its linker script is zephyr's stock generic
# arm64 one. It carries no QEMU-specific assumptions. It is already reused
# by the qemu_kvm_arm64 board (a real-AArch64/HW-virtualization target, not
# software emulation) for exactly this reason. We reuse it here rather than
# duplicating a whole new (also-generic) SoC layer for one board.

config BOARD_BPI_M64_HV
	select SOC_QEMU_VIRT_ARM64
